@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: WWW Landing Pages
	Frontend testing for creating a landing page on www

Setup:
    * I get all test passwords and admin emails

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I sign out and sign into www as a user with the email address "${staticWWWAdminEmailAddress}" and password "${staticWWWAdminPassword}"
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I go to the www page with the url "web/l"
	* I tear down the following pages
	| Test Event1 Page |
	| Test Event2 Page |

Scenario: Add Landing Page With Removed Section
	Admins should be able to add a landing page on www with a removed section.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	And I click on the Sign In Create Account footer link
	And I sign into www as a user with the email address "${staticWWWAdminEmailAddress}" and password "${staticWWWAdminPassword}"
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	And I go to the www page with the url "web/l"
	And I navigate to the Product Menu and go to the "Pages" portlet under the "Site Builder" category under the "Site Administration" panel
	And I click on the add public page button
	And I click on the "Event - Thank You" page template
	And I add a public page with the name "Test Event1 Page"
	And I go to the "Selection" editor sidebar category
	And I remove the section in position "2"
	And I click on the publish public page button
	Then I should be able to view the public page "Test Event1 Page"

Scenario: Add Landing Page With Added Section
	Admins should be able to add a landing page on www with an added section.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	And I click on the Sign In Create Account footer link
	And I sign into www as a user with the email address "${staticWWWAdminEmailAddress}" and password "${staticWWWAdminPassword}"
	And I wait for "5" seconds
	And I go to the www page with the url "web/l"
	And I navigate to the Product Menu and go to the "Pages" portlet under the "Site Builder" category under the "Site Administration" panel
	And I click on the add public page button
	And I click on the "Event - Thank You" page template
	And I add a public page with the name "Test Event2 Page"
	And I drag and drop the card labeled "Form Callout" within the "Fragments and Widgets" sidebar category under the "Landing Page Components" panel group above the section in position "2"
	And I click on the publish public page button
	Then I should be able to view the public page "Test Event2 Page"